D3D12, validation: a non-array texture view of a layer other than the first is refused.

D3D12's non-array 1D, 2D and 2DMS views and its cube view have no array slice, so
DescriptorD3D12::Create drops TextureViewDesc::layerOffset for TEXTURE, SUBPASS_INPUT,
STORAGE_TEXTURE and TEXTURE_CUBE views of a 1D or 2D texture, and the view addresses the first layer
(or cube) without a word. Vulkan honours it (baseArrayLayer). An array view would not match the
shader's non-array declaration, so D3D12 cannot express such a view. Since 0c5f574 (initial commit).

This refuses it in NRI validation on every backend, pointing to the "_ARRAY" view types, which
address any layer on both backends. The backend is left alone: public-input checks belong to
Validation (.agents/skills/nri-coding-standard).
Measured on v190, NVIDIA: a two-layer texture, a STORAGE_TEXTURE view with layerOffset 1,
CmdClearStorage: Vulkan cleared layer 1, D3D12 layer 0, with no message from NRI validation or
either backend's layer. With the change, TEXTURE and STORAGE_TEXTURE views with layerOffset 1 and a
TEXTURE_CUBE view with layerOffset 6 are refused with INVALID_ARGUMENT and one error naming
"layerOffset" and "_ARRAY", on both backends with NRI validation; the same views of the first layer
are created.

diff --git a/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp b/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp
index 0bb2a05..3232ce4 100644
--- a/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp
+++ b/Source/Validation/DeviceVal.hpp
@@ -394,6 +394,10 @@ NRI_INLINE Result DeviceVal::CreateDescriptor(const TextureViewDesc& textureView
     NRI_RETURN_ON_FAILURE(this, textureViewDesc.layerOffset + layerNum <= textureDesc.layerNum, Result::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
         "'layerOffset=%u' + 'layerNum=%u' must be <= texture 'layerNum=%u'", textureViewDesc.layerOffset, layerNum, textureDesc.layerNum);
 
+    bool isNonArrayView = textureViewDesc.type == TextureView::TEXTURE || textureViewDesc.type == TextureView::SUBPASS_INPUT || textureViewDesc.type == TextureView::STORAGE_TEXTURE || textureViewDesc.type == TextureView::TEXTURE_CUBE;
+    NRI_RETURN_ON_FAILURE(this, textureDesc.type == TextureType::TEXTURE_3D || !isNonArrayView || textureViewDesc.layerOffset == 0, Result::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
+        "'layerOffset=%u' must be 0 for a non-array 'viewType' (D3D12 can't select a layer there), use the '_ARRAY' view type", textureViewDesc.layerOffset);
+
     NRI_RETURN_ON_FAILURE(this, textureViewDesc.sliceOffset + sliceNum <= textureDesc.depth, Result::INVALID_ARGUMENT,
         "'sliceOffset=%u' + 'sliceNum=%u' must be <= texture 'depth=%u'", textureViewDesc.sliceOffset, sliceNum, textureDesc.depth);
 
